{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>My firstborn son is Israel.</b> All the nations are sons, but Israel is beloved before Him more than all of them, and they are the firstborn, for they arose in thought to be created before any nation. Another interpretation: <b>My firstborn son is Israel</b> — whence did the matter come that Jacob acquired the birthright from Esau his brother, and it was given to him? And before Aaron was chosen for the priesthood, the divine service was among the firstborn; therefore He said: 'Send My son that he may serve Me,' because he is the firstborn."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:08.621231145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}